@startuml physical-view-airports-routes
skinparam shadowing false
title Airports & Routes - physical view (Mode B, docker-compose.secure.yml)

node "Docker host" {
  node "edge network" {
    node "gateway-1\nnginx :8443" as G1
    node "gateway-2\nnginx :8444" as G2
    node "rabbitmq\nrabbitmq:3-management\nmgmt UI 127.0.0.1:15672" as RB
  }
  node "backend network (internal, no Internet)" {
    node "keycloak-1" as K1
    node "keycloak-2" as K2
    database "keycloak-db\nPostgreSQL 16" as KDB

    node "airports-routes-1\nSpring Boot :8443 (HTTPS)" as AR1
    database "airports-db-1\nPostgreSQL 16\n(write model + read model)" as DB1
    node "airports-routes-2\nSpring Boot :8443 (HTTPS)" as AR2
    database "airports-db-2\nPostgreSQL 16\n(write model + read model)" as DB2

    node "aircraft-1 / -2\nmaintenance-1 / -2\nflight-operations-1 / -2" as OTHER
  }
}

actor "Client" as C
C --> G1 : HTTPS
C --> G2 : HTTPS (2nd entry point)
G1 --> AR1 : HTTPS (round-robin)
G1 --> AR2
G2 --> AR1
G2 --> AR2
G1 --> K1
G1 --> K2
K1 --> KDB : JDBC
K2 --> KDB : JDBC

AR1 --> DB1 : JDBC
AR2 --> DB2 : JDBC
AR1 --> RB : AMQP :5672
AR2 --> RB : AMQP :5672
OTHER --> RB : AMQP :5672
AR1 <..> AR2 : HTTPS\nP2P read forwarding (X-P2P-Hops)

note bottom of DB1
  Database-per-Service pattern: a dedicated
  PostgreSQL instance per service instance.
  Data isolation: replicas never share a database;
  state converges through AMQP events only.
end note

note right of RB
  Single broker in Mode B. Queues are durable,
  so events survive a broker restart; if the
  broker is down, writes keep working and the
  outbox retries publication (up to 10 attempts,
  exponential backoff capped at 60 s).
end note
@enduml
